This repository is an independent, skill-native port of PaperOrchestra:
  PaperOrchestra: A Multi-Agent Framework for Automated AI Research Paper Writing
  Yiwen Song, Yale Song, Tomas Pfister, Jinsung Yoon
  Google Cloud AI Research
  https://github.com/google-research/paper-orchestra
  Copyright 2026 Google LLC
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The following material is adapted from that repository and remains under the
Apache License, Version 2.0:
  - the five-stage pipeline design and agent responsibilities;
  - outline, literature review, section writing, content refinement, and
    plotting prompt directives;
  - the citation verification policy, reviewer rubric, and evaluation concepts;
  - the CVPR 2025 and ICLR 2025 template bundles under
    skills/paper-template/assets/templates/.

The conference style files (*.sty, *.bst) are the official files distributed
with each venue's author kit and remain subject to their original terms. Their
copyright headers are preserved.

The scripts in this repository are a clean-room reimplementation using the
Python standard library unless a dependency is explicitly documented.
